WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.137 --> 00:00:03.462
- It's five in the morning. Woo!

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:04.673
(light piano music)

00:00:06.433 --> 00:00:09.603
Today we are going to the River Ganges

00:00:09.603 --> 00:00:11.623
to perform the last rites ceremony

00:00:11.623 --> 00:00:16.623
for my grandfather, and deposit
his ashes into the river.

00:00:16.662 --> 00:00:19.554
It's such a difference
from New Delhi yesterday,

00:00:19.554 --> 00:00:22.177
because that was like totally yang

00:00:22.177 --> 00:00:23.883
and this it totally yin.

00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:26.542
One thing that I struggle with a lot

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:29.679
is like worrying, over-planning.

00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:32.000
Today I saw something so special

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.157
in the unique fusion of
messiness and beauty.

00:00:36.157 --> 00:00:40.549
All the crazy wild animals,
and then this happened.

00:00:40.549 --> 00:00:42.720
There's a cow, right there.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.870
Seeing all the crowds of people.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.415
And this bridge.

00:00:46.415 --> 00:00:48.422
This looks like a storybook!

00:00:48.422 --> 00:00:50.364
Can you guys feel the bridge moving?

00:00:50.364 --> 00:00:52.976
- I was here when I was three years old.

00:00:52.976 --> 00:00:57.180
And I remember vaguely that
I had a really hard time

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.561
getting on the bridge
because I was so scared.

00:00:59.561 --> 00:01:03.136
And my father just grabbed
me and I was screaming,

00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:04.704
and he took me across (laughs).

00:01:04.704 --> 00:01:07.398
- I was expecting the last rites ceremony

00:01:07.398 --> 00:01:09.894
to be very sad, but I was surprised

00:01:09.894 --> 00:01:12.424
with how much peace
and closure it gave me.

00:01:12.424 --> 00:01:14.818
The tragic event of my
grandfather's sudden death

00:01:14.818 --> 00:01:17.058
incited my first trip to India,

00:01:17.058 --> 00:01:19.020
and in coming here I have seen a glimpse

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.648
into the hard work and sacrifices

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:24.687
my grandfather made to create
the best life for our family.

00:01:24.687 --> 00:01:27.196
I feel a responsibility
now to work even harder

00:01:27.196 --> 00:01:29.669
for my dreams, and to fulfill the path

00:01:29.669 --> 00:01:31.388
that my grandfather paved for me.

00:01:31.388 --> 00:01:35.010
We just finished the
ceremony for my grandfather.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.439
Really glad I came to do it.

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:41.844
I feel some closure,

00:01:41.844 --> 00:01:44.305
but I'm still processing.

00:01:44.305 --> 00:01:47.168
I love how colorful this country is,

00:01:47.168 --> 00:01:49.943
both literally and metaphorically.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:52.045
How in this culture, something as sad,

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:55.158
terrifying, and mournful
as someone's death

00:01:55.158 --> 00:01:59.553
is remembered in a beautiful
celebration of their life.

00:01:59.553 --> 00:02:03.374
You never really know
how special something

00:02:03.374 --> 00:02:06.370
or someone is until they're gone.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.296
Sometimes you have to travel halfway

00:02:08.296 --> 00:02:10.131
around the world to discover that.

00:02:10.131 --> 00:02:13.091
I challenge you today to tell a friend

00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:16.597
or a family member how much
you love and appreciate them.

00:02:16.597 --> 00:02:18.618
Because you might not even be aware

00:02:18.618 --> 00:02:20.197
of the sacrifices they have made

00:02:20.197 --> 00:02:22.921
for you until they're gone.

